        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_984658505.1",
        "comments": "The assembly dcRumAceo1.hap1.1 is based on 53x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The assembly shows a complex polyploid structure, comprising three diploid chromosome sets, three tetraploid chromosome sets, and four hexaploid chromosome sets. Partial homology is observed between the diploid and tetraploid chromosome groups. Due to the complex and overlapping homology patterns observed across the assembly, all chromosomes have been retained within a single assembly representation rather than separated into alternative haplotypes or subgenomes.",
